Now I have all the data. Here's the full academic audit.

---

## Test Smell Audit — `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`

**Framework:** MSTest 4.1 · **.NET 10** · **Scope:** `[TestCategory("Integration")]`
**Catalog:** testsmells.org 19-smell taxonomy (Peruma et al., ESEC/FSE 2020)

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 3           | 3              |
| Medium   | 1           | 1              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4 / 8**      |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### ❶ Conditional Test Logic — High

**Smell:** `if`/`else` inside the test changes which assertion runs; one branch may never execute, hiding a gap.

**Affected:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 101–108)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);   // ← only runs if PremiumUser
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);       // ← only runs otherwise
}
```

**Fix — split into two explicit tests:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenStandard_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");
    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenPremium_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("eve@example.com", "Eve", discountRate: 0.1m));
    var loaded = (PremiumUser)_repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com")!;
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** If `GetByEmail` never returns a `PremiumUser`, the discount assertion is dead code — you'll never know it's broken.

---

#### ❷ Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test) — High

**Smell:** The test exercises code but never asserts a result. The test framework reports a pass as long as no exception is thrown, providing false confidence.

**Affected:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (lines 113–119)

```csharp
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
    // ← no assertion
}
```

> **Calibration note:** The method name implies a "does not throw" intent, which is a weak implicit assertion. Still flagged — the test should verify something observable.

**Fix — assert the observable outcome:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Insert could silently drop rows, corrupt data, or ignore duplicates — this test would still pass.

---

#### ❸ Sleepy Test — High

**Smell:** `Thread.Sleep` introduces a hard 3-second wall-clock wait. The delay is non-deterministic (may be too short on slow CI, always too long on fast hardware) and inflates suite runtime.

**Affected:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 87)

```csharp
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    Thread.Sleep(3000);   // ← hard 3-second sleep

    Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
}
```

> **Integration calibration:** Async coordination delays are *more common* in integration tests, but `Thread.Sleep` is still a smell even here — it couples test reliability to arbitrary timing.

**Fix — poll with a timeout or use an event-based wait:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    // Poll with back-off instead of a fixed sleep
    var deadline = DateTime.UtcNow.AddSeconds(5);
    while (DateTime.UtcNow < deadline)
    {
        if (_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
            break;
        await Task.Delay(100);
    }

    Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
}
```

Alternatively, if the notification mechanism supports it, expose a `Task` or `ManualResetEventSlim` the test can `await` directly.

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky failures in CI (slow runners exceed 3 s); wasted time locally (3 s per run even when notification is instant).

---

#### ❹ Assertion Roulette — Medium

**Smell:** Multiple assertions without descriptive failure messages. When one fails, the runner reports a line number but no human-readable context.

**Affected:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (lines 35–38)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

Four assertions, zero messages — a failure reads: *"Assert.AreEqual failed. Expected:<Alice>. Actual:<(null)>."* — which property? Which test scenario?

**Fix — add message parameters:**

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Id should be assigned by the database");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slow diagnosis when a failure occurs — especially in CI logs where you can't set breakpoints.

---

### Smell-Free Patterns ✅

Four of eight tests are clean and well-structured:

| Test | Why it's good |
|------|--------------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear arrange/act/assert, focused assertions |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Single behavior, concise null-check assertion |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Count (3) is self-documenting after 3 inserts; `CollectionAssert` is appropriate |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Good concurrency test; count (10) matches the `Range(0,10)` — no magic number |

The `[TestInitialize]`/`[TestCleanup]` fixture is **not** over-broad (General Fixture) — both `_connection` and `_repository` are used by every test.

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Effort |
|----------|-------|-----|--------|
| 1 | **Assertion-Free Test** — `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` | Add `Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count)` | 2 min |
| 2 | **Conditional Test Logic** — `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` | Split into two deterministic tests | 10 min |
| 3 | **Sleepy Test** — `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with poll-loop or event wait | 15 min |
| 4 | **Assertion Roulette** — `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` | Add message strings to each `Assert` call | 2 min |

Priorities 1–2 prevent **false-pass risk** (tests that look green but verify nothing meaningful). Priority 3 prevents **flaky failures**. Priority 4 is a **diagnostic quality** improvement.
